46,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NDM0Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/664346?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz","html_url":"https://github.com/kmarcisz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kmarcisz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-15T00:53:32Z","updated_at":"2026-07-15T00:53:32Z","body":"Same here, some of our tests are over 5s and we would like the per-test override be available in bunfig.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oven-sh/bun/issues/comments/4975639725/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oven-sh/bun/issues/comments/5543573934","html_url":"https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/7789#issuecomment-5543573934","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oven-sh/bun/issues/7789","id":5543573934,"node_id":"IC_kwDOFVKCyc8AAAABSmw5rg","user":{"login":"code-yeongyu","id":11153873,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTUzODcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11153873?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu","html_url":"https://github.com/code-yeongyu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/code-yeongyu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-04T16:35:03Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T16:35:03Z","body":"Reproduced on 1.4.0 (also 1.4.1), and adding a data point on why this matters more than a convenience.\n\n`setDefaultTimeout` is documented as file-scoped, and a preload only runs once per process — so a preload that calls it raises the budget for the **first** test file only; every later file in a sequential `bun test` run falls back to 5000ms. Minimal repro:\n\n```\nmkdir -p repro/probe && cd repro\nprintf '[test]\\npreload = [\"./setup.ts\"]\\n' > bunfig.toml\nprintf 'import { setDefaultTimeout } from \"bun:test\"\\nsetDefaultTimeout(20_000)\\n' > setup.ts\nfor n in a b c; do printf 'import { test, expect } from \"bun:test\"\\ntest(\"%s\", async () => { await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 6500)); expect(true).toBe(true) })\\n' $n > probe/$n.test.ts; done\nbun test probe            # 1 pass / 2 fail  (b,c: \"timed out after 5000ms\")\nbun test --parallel probe # 3 pass  (each worker re-runs the preload)\nbun test --timeout 20000 probe  # 3 pass\n```\n\nThe natural place to set a repo-wide default is `[test] timeout` in bunfig.toml — but as reported here it is silently ignored: with `timeout = 20000` in `[test]` the run above is still 1 pass / 2 fail on 1.4.0. So today the only mechanism that reaches every file is the CLI flag, which has to be repeated at every `bun test` call site in CI.\n\nReal-world impact: a monorepo preload raising the CI floor to 30s on windows-latest silently protected one file per job; a 9.3s test died at 5000ms and was chased as a Windows flake for weeks. A parsed `[test] timeout` (or a documented note that a preload's `setDefaultTimeout` is first-file-only) would have made that a one-line fix.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oven-sh/bun/issues/comments/5543573934/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]